As promised, the alpha version for nfss slitex addaption.

cheers Frank



README file: 92/01/10 FMi

This slitex implementation of NFSS is a non-official alpha testing
version.  No garantie whatsoever is given that any of the implemented
features and misfeatures will survive in the first release.  It is
therefore only for testing purposes. Nevertheless please report bugs
and suggestions.

Files of NFSS for slitex:

  sfonts.new            to be used instead of sfonts.tex
  slitex.doc            to be used instead of slitex.tex
  sfontdef.doc		a font definition example file. You may want
                        to make your own variant
  nwslides.doc		a document styles to be used instead of slides.sty
			There isn't much of documentation, just some
                        comments from the time when I made this
                        version, but you must rename the file to .sty


All other files can be used from the offical NFSS, that is oldlfont
and newlfont etc will work. To make a format one can use preload.min,
(but using preload.ori of course will not work:-) and basefont, or
oldlfont or newlfont.

Using nwslides instead of slides should work with a format using the
old sfonts. However one needs to remake the format because slitex has
changed.


Open problems:

  1) nwslides is made from an older slides.doc version and therefore
misses some of the updates. Same for slitex.

  2) The \set@font@size@parms function may need a
belowshortdisplayskip parameter. On the other hand it may not, as a
style that really wants to set it could do so after calling it.

  3) I made something like an interface to the old sfonts.tex. But I
couldn't test it very well because of the lack of suitable slide
sources that do not make use of advantages of NFSS. Therefore it may
contain a good number of errors and also may be unexeptable for other
reasons. You try please.

 4) This is alpha testing so be prepared for errors (and overfull
hboxes Phil :-)


Happy trying

Frank


